# spec: when the current CNC step is one of the new presets, set_cnc_presets selects that preset's index. While ANC is off it switches ANC on first, since the 700 refuses a [1.15] write then; it writes the step back while ANC is on, because a [1.5] write that switches ANC on or off ignores its step, and then switches ANC off.
# source: hardware report on firmware 1.8.2-11524+e0f7590: with [1.5] = 0b0000, SETGET [1.15] answered ERROR 06 InvalidData; SETGET [1.5] 0001 on 0b0000 returned 0b0301 (the selected preset), and 0000 on 0b0501 returned 0b0500. The sequence on, [1.15], step back, off on 0b0200 ended at 0b0200. The replies are synthetic, following those layouts.
device nc700
call set_cnc_presets 0 5 10
send 01 05 01 00
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 05 00
send 01 05 02 02 05 01
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 00 01
send 01 0f 02 04 01 00 05 0a
recv 01 0f 03 04 01 00 05 0a
send 01 05 02 02 05 01
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 05 01
send 01 05 02 02 05 00
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 05 00
result ok
